  abstract={A  $W$ -band metallic waveguide module capable of spatial power combining of linear microstrip array is presented. The module employs two uniquely devised split-channel blocks to obtain a uniform field distribution in an oversize merged channel and couple an equal amount of power to ten microstrip elements aligned in the direction of the waveguide  $E$ -plane. The array of microstrip thru lines, each with a pair of bonding wires, is fabricated on a single dielectric substrate. The measurements indicate that the merged-channel power-combining scheme is properly operating as the two modules separately built to house single and array elements show similar frequency response with flat insertion losses of 2–3 dB between 90 and 98 GHz.},
